  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Kenya Market Assistance Programme (MAP)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">To reduce poverty in Kenya by enabling poor people to benefit from better functioning markets, and by building greater awareness among influential decision makers of how markets can work better for the poor. This will increase household incomes of 148,000 small scale farmers and entrepreneurs - of whom 33% are women - by an average of over 20% by 2018. 36,000 jobs for women and 73,000 for men and male youth will also be created.</narrative>
  </description>
